    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and working. Here's what I did:\n\n## Problem\nThe `--ci` flag wasn't being passed through from the `frai` CLI to the `frai-gate` CLI. This was happening because Commander.js was parsing the `--ci` option at the parent command level (where it's defined as an option) and not passing it to the gate subcommand.\n\n## Solution\nI modified the `gate` command's action handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to reconstruct the arguments from the raw `process.argv` instead of relying on Commander's parsed arguments. This ensures all original flags are forwarded to the frai-gate CLI.\n\nThe key change:\n- **Before**: Used the `args` parameter which had already been processed by Commander\n- **After**: Extract arguments directly from `process.argv` starting from the `gate` command, preserving all flags\n\n## Verification\nAfter rebuilding with `pnpm --filter frai build`, I tested the command and confirmed both files are now created:\n- \u2705 `FRAI-SPEC.md` \n- \u2705 `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n\nThe workflow file creation now correctly depends on the `--ci` flag being passed through the frai CLI.",
